/** @page kalmanrelease kalman Module Release History

    @tableofcontents

    @section kalman_1_1 kalman Module Version 1.1
    - Pre-baked model factories for common tracking cases:
      @ref Qore::Kalman::newConstantVelocity2D()
      "newConstantVelocity2D()", @ref
      Qore::Kalman::newConstantAcceleration2D()
      "newConstantAcceleration2D()", and
      @ref Qore::Kalman::newGpsSmoother() "newGpsSmoother()". Each
      returns a fully-configured @ref Qore::Kalman::LinearFilter
      "LinearFilter" ready to step — no manual F / H / Q / R
      construction needed for the 90% case.
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::LinearFilter::stepBatch()
      "LinearFilter::stepBatch()" — bulk predict+update across an
      observation list in one call, cheaper than N Qore round-trips.
      Checks for cooperative cancellation between iterations so
      long batches remain killable via @c cancel_thread() or
      @c SandboxManager::requestInterrupt().
    - Release notes: UKF (unscented Kalman filter) and filter-state
      serialization are planned for 1.2. 1.1 focuses on the business-
      use-case helpers and the batch step operation.

    @section kalman_1_0 kalman Module Version 1.0
    - initial public release
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::Matrix "Matrix" primitive with arithmetic,
      transpose, inverse, cholesky, determinant
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::LinearFilter "LinearFilter" (standard KF)
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::ExtendedFilter "ExtendedFilter" (EKF via
      Qore Jacobian callbacks)
    - Joseph-form covariance update for numerical stability
    - module version helpers
*/
